---
title: Ham And Pasta Bake
servings: 6
cuisine: american
main_protein: pork
prep_time: "20 minutes"
cook_time: "30 minutes"
tags:
  - dinner
  - ham
  - pasta
  - broccoli
  - cheese
  - comfort
leftover_portions: 2
prep:
  - Preheat oven to 350°F
  - Bring 3 qts water to a boil
  - Dice 2 cups cooked ham
  - Grate 0.75 cup cheddar cheese
---

Cook @elbow macaroni{2%cups} in first amount of boiling @water{3%qts}, @cooking oil{1%tbsp} (optional) and @salt{2%tsp} in #large saucepan{}, uncovered, for ~{5%minutes} to 7 minutes until tender but firm. Drain.

Combine @all-purpose flour{0.25%cup}, @salt{1%tsp}, @black pepper{0.125%tsp}, @dry mustard{0.5%tsp} and @onion flakes{1%tbsp} in #medium saucepan{}. Gradually mix in @milk{2.5%cups} so no lumps remain. Heat and stir until boiling and thickened.

Cook @frozen chopped broccoli{10%oz} in second amount of boiling @water{} (to cover) until tender-crisp. Drain. Add to sauce. Stir in macaroni.

Add @cooked ham{2%cups}, diced or cubed (about 0.75 lb), and @cheddar cheese{0.75%cup}, grated (medium or sharp). Stir. Turn into ungreased 2 quart (2 L) #casserole dish{}.

Topping: Melt @margarine{2%tbsp} (or butter) in saucepan. Stir in @fine dry bread crumbs{0.5%cup}. Sprinkle over all. Bake in 350°F (175°C) #oven{} for about ~{30%minutes} until browned. Serves 6.

-- Source: image of physical recipe
-- An attractive meal-in-one dish. This is a casserole that can be baked one day and reheated and served the next, or even frozen. Flavor is even better when reheated.
-- 1 serving: 428 Calories; 27 g Protein; 14 g Total Fat; 49 g Carbohydrate; 1540 mg Sodium
